            "target_entity_instance": "Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "westerlies produces an intensification of the northern branch of the North Pacific Gyre, which is stronger on the eastern part compared to the western part. This tends (i) to trans- port the warmer water from the northern extension of the Kuroshio eastward (around 45\u00b0 N).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Gulf Stream current",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
